The attached image, Figure 6, illustrates how Nano-11 enhances antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and increases antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) express the highest levels of CD86, crucial for T-cell activation. Panel B further characterizes these cells, indicating that OVA is primarily found in CD11b+ DCs following Nano-11 adjuvant. Panel C, using in vivo imaging, demonstrates that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide, prolongs antigen retention at the injection site over several days compared to soluble antigen, ensuring sustained antigen availability for immune cell uptake.